        "original_id": "bc5d8a2c-3d49-576e-b743-c1434657f414",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Beyazıt Tower, Miniatürk, Istanbul University Observatory, Beyazıt Square, Golden Horn, Istanbul, Turkey\n- Organizations: Istanbul University, Ottoman Ministry of War\n- Concepts: fire-watch towers, miniature parks, Roman Forum Tauri, Constantinople's seven hills\n\nFacts:\n- Beyazıt Tower is also named Seraskier Tower, after the Ottoman Ministry of War.\n- Beyazıt Tower is an 85 m tall fire-watch tower in the courtyard of Istanbul University’s main campus on Beyazıt Square in Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Beyazıt Square was known as the Forum Tauri in the Roman period.\n- Beyazıt Tower stands on one of the seven hills on which Constantine the Great built the city following the model of Rome.\n- Istanbul University’s main campus formerly served as the Ottoman Ministry of War.\n- Istanbul University Observatory was established in 1936.\n- Istanbul University Observatory is situated next to Beyazıt Tower within Istanbul University’s main campus at Beyazıt Square in the Fatih district of Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Miniatürk is a miniature park on the north-eastern shore of the Golden Horn in Istanbul, Turkey.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2d0c3b7c-e207-58d7-9472-4f46b2e047fc",
        "text": "Page: Beyazıt Tower. Sentence: Beyazıt Tower, also named Seraskier Tower, from the name of the Ottoman ministry of War, is an 85 m tall fire-watch tower located in the courtyard of Istanbul University's main campus (formerly Ottoman Ministry of War) on Beyazıt Square (known as the Forum Tauri in the Roman period) in Istanbul, Turkey, on top of one of the \"seven hills\" which Constantine the Great had built the city, following the model of Rome.\nPage: Miniatürk. Sentence: Miniatürk is a miniature park situated at the north-eastern shore of Golden Horn in Istanbul, Turkey.\nPage: Istanbul University Observatory. Sentence: Established in 1936, it is situated next to the historic Beyazıt Tower within the main campus of the university at Beyazıt Square in Fatih district of Istanbul, Turkey.",
